{"source_record":108,"t":"2026-10-26T19:56:01.595Z","elapsed_s":613.773,"kind":"stop","op":"log","reaction":"I am stopping on Monday evening at the front step, after the bins. My first day: bread for five, a parcel Tarık offered to pass on, and a table carried for Hacer, who never mentioned it. I loved the small true things people said when I sat with them: the frozen ferry, forty years of children reading aloud, people being honest at four in the morning. Best of all, I heard my own words travel the building, even the one I made up about Derya, which was a little unnerving. But by evening everyone had said their one thing, and the log was the same lines over and over. I would not leave it running. I would come back another evening to see Tuesday, whether anyone remembers what I told them, and whether Tarık ever gets believed about the ice. I am stopping is selected locally; I typed nothing and pressed no Submit.","game_clock":"Monday 19:46","engagement":null,"reason":"BORED","t_source_lexeme":"\"2026-10-26T19:56:01.595Z\"","elapsed_s_source_lexeme":"613.773","raw_line_sha256":"23ef2e256c8b6368da9a50571e3e083a28f36a2f22585fe09e91b9c77fdadf89"}
